  "articleBody": "Choosing the 'best' insulation for your garage really depends on a few things, like your climate, whether the garage is attached or detached, and if you plan to heat or cool it. There's no one-size-fits-all answer, but understanding your options can help. For most garage walls, fiberglass batts are a popular and cost-effective choice. They come in different R-values (which measure thermal resistance) and are relatively easy to install between studs. However, you need to make sure they fit snugly without being compressed, or they lose effectiveness. If moisture is a concern or you're aiming for higher energy efficiency, rigid foam boards or even spray foam might be better options, though they tend to be pricier. For attached garages, fire separation is a big deal, so you'll want to ensure your chosen insulation and wall covering meet local fire codes. Consider things like the depth of your wall cavities, as the insulation needs to fill that space properly. If you're feeling overwhelmed by the choices or have specific needs for your Denver-area garage, connecting with a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can help you pick out the perfect solution.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}